@startuml
!theme plain
title Trip Score Model - Explainable Fleet Score From Risk Events

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #19226D

rectangle "Risk events\nlabel, severity, confidence,\nstart/end timestamp,\nevidence frame" as Events #F37021
rectangle "Context features\nspeed, road type, turn signal,\ntraffic density, driver state" as Context #EAF2FF
rectangle "Event consolidation\nmerge repeated alerts\nsuppress flicker" as Merge #FFFFFF
rectangle "Penalty model\nseverity x duration x confidence\nwith context multiplier" as Penalty #FFFFFF
rectangle "Learned calibration\nGBDT / logistic calibration\nmaps event mix -> trip risk" as Learned #FFFFFF
rectangle "Score composer\n100 - capped penalties\n+ recovery / safe-driving credits" as Composer #034EA2
rectangle "Score breakdown\nroad risk, driver state,\nvehicle handling, lane behavior" as Breakdown #FFFFFF
rectangle "Post-trip report\nwhy score changed\nwhat to coach next" as Report #EAF2FF

Events --> Merge
Context --> Penalty
Merge --> Penalty
Penalty --> Learned
Learned --> Composer
Composer --> Breakdown
Breakdown --> Report

note right of Composer
Recommended MVP:
Use interpretable additive score for demo,
then learn calibration weights from labeled trips.
This gives both explainability and adaptability.
end note

@enduml
